---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';import ProjectCard from '../../components/ProjectCard.astro';import {projects} from '../../data/projects';import {url} from '../../lib/url';
import CaseScreenshots from '../../components/CaseScreenshots.astro';
export function getStaticPaths(){return projects.map(project=>({params:{slug:project.id},props:{project}}));}
const {project:p}=Astro.props;
const labels:Record<string,string>={repo:'View source on GitHub',stable:'Stable release',preview:'Preview release',apk:'Download stable Android APK',windows:'Download stable Windows installer',previewApk:'Download preview APK',previewWindows:'Download preview Windows installer',checksum:'Stable APK SHA-256 checksum',releaseHistory:'Release history',architecture:'Repository architecture diagram',demo:'Open project demo'};
const food=p.title==='Food Fight';const team=p.title==='TeamSync SaaS';const rice=p.title==='Ittehad Food Industries';
---
<Base title={`${p.title} — Muhammad Irfan Waseem`} description={p.description}><header class="page-head wrap"><a class="text-link" href={url('projects/')}>All projects</a><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:32px">{p.label} · {p.status}</p><h1>{p.title}</h1><p>{p.description}</p></header><div class="wrap case-hero"><ProjectCard project={p}/></div><div class="wrap case-content"><article class="prose"><section><h2>The problem</h2><p>{p.problem}</p></section><section><h2>My contribution</h2><p>{p.role}</p></section><section><h2>Scope & implementation</h2><p>{p.description}</p>{p.features.length>0 && <ul>{p.features.map(feature=><li>{feature}</li>)}</ul>}{food && <><p>Customers build a cart and confirm a server-validated quote. Branch staff prepare orders and dispatch riders; riders confirm pickup, delivery and cash collection.</p><p>Firebase Authentication establishes identity. Cloud Functions and Firestore rules enforce role and branch permissions. Backend functions handle checkout, order transitions, dispatch and cash settlement.</p><div class="architecture" aria-label="Food Fight architecture"><span>Flutter role workspaces</span><span>Firebase Authentication</span><span>Functions & access rules</span><span>Firestore & notifications</span></div><h3>Engineering considerations</h3><p>Checkout revalidates catalog prices and availability on the server. Reusing a checkout request ID can return the existing order. Cash on Delivery is the documented payment method; maps, SMS and optional uploads depend on platform configuration.</p></>}{team && <><p>The repository separates a React and TypeScript client from an Express API and MongoDB data layer. Workspaces group projects and tasks, with Owner, Admin and Member permissions.</p><div class="architecture"><span>React client</span><span>Express API</span><span>Workspace permissions</span><span>MongoDB / Mongoose</span></div><h3>Engineering considerations</h3><p>Workspace isolation and role permissions are central to the design. The README documents cookie-based sessions and Mongoose transactions for consistent multi-document changes.</p><p>Billing, real-time notifications and a workspace activity timeline are roadmap items, rather than released features.</p></>}{rice && <><p>The documented workflow connects paddy procurement, processing batches, stock, customer ordering and logistics. Flutter presents role-specific modules backed by Firebase, with Supabase described for media storage.</p><div class="architecture"><span>Procurement</span><span>Processing</span><span>Inventory</span><span>Sales & logistics</span></div><h3>Project boundaries</h3><p>This is the Ittehad Food Industries source repository. It is not presented as a separately verified MillX ERP release. Production deployment and measured business outcomes have not been independently verified.</p></>}</section><section><h2>Current outcome</h2><p>{p.result}</p><p class="notice">Status: {p.status}. Repository documentation establishes scope; it does not establish user counts, revenue or production adoption.</p></section><section><h2>Project media</h2><p>{p.image?'The cover uses a supplied project screenshot.':'The cover is an original concept illustration, not a screenshot of running software.'} Source links provide further implementation context.</p></section><section><h2>Explore further</h2><p>Review the repository for setup instructions, source files and the latest development activity.</p><a class="button quiet" href={url('projects/')}>Back to all projects</a></section></article><aside class="case-aside"><h2>Technology</h2><div class="tags">{p.tags.map(tag=><span>{tag}</span>)}</div><h2 style="margin-top:35px">Source & downloads</h2>{Object.entries(p.links).map(([key,href])=><a href={href} rel="noopener noreferrer">{labels[key]||key}</a>)}{food && <p class="notice">Stable and preview channels are separate. The Windows installer is unsigned, as documented by the project.</p>}</aside></div><CaseScreenshots slug={p.id}/></Base>
